# Design & Mockup Implementation Rules

## Intent
Ensure mockup implementations are grounded in existing features, preventing technical debt and scope creep caused by AI-generated designs that may include features not yet built.

## Core Rule: Existing Features Only
- The Replit design submodule (`design/`) is produced by an AI agent. It frequently includes UI for features that **do not yet exist** in the codebase.
- **Never implement UI, layout, or interactions for features that have no corresponding backend API, database table, or working server-side logic.**
- **Never add stub data, mock data arrays, or hardcoded placeholder values** to production shells to satisfy a mockup. If the shell needs data, it must come from a real API endpoint.
- If a mockup element requires a feature that doesn't exist, **stop and ask the user** whether they want to scope that feature before implementing any part of it.

## Allowed: Pixel-Perfect Visual Updates
These changes are safe to implement without asking:
- Colors, typography, spacing, border-radius, gradients matching the mockup
- Layout structure (grid, flex, icon rail widths, sidebar widths) for **existing** shell components
- Icon choices, badge text, section labels — for already-implemented sections
- Responsive breakpoints and media queries
- CSS variable / design token updates in `globals.css`
- Empty-state copy and visual treatment for features already wired up

## Blocked Without User Approval
Before implementing any of the following, stop and ask:
- Any new API call not already present in the shell file being updated
- Any UI section that references data from an API endpoint that doesn't exist in `ctf/packages/web/app/api/`
- New interactive features (tabs, drawers, modals) backed by data that isn't already fetched
- New pages or routes not already defined under `ctf/packages/web/app/`
- New plugin shells not already present under `ctf/packages/web/components/`

## Audit Process
When implementing mockups:
1. For each mockup component, list every data requirement (API calls, props, state).
2. Cross-check each requirement against existing API routes (`ctf/packages/web/app/api/`).
3. Mark each requirement as **Exists** or **Missing**.
4. Implement only **Exists** sections; surface **Missing** ones to the user as a prioritized list.

## No Stub Data Policy
- Do not introduce `const STATIC_DATA = [...]` arrays or hardcoded objects into production shell components.
- If a section cannot be rendered without real data, render a clean empty/loading state until the API exists.
- Exception: the `design/` submodule itself may use stub data for mockup previews — this is expected and should not be copied into `ctf/`.
